sentences.i:
I swear by his cheek and the smile of his mouth, and by the arrows he has fledged with his enchantment;
by the suppleness of his flanks and the keen blade of his glance, by the whiteness of his brow and the blackness of his hair;
by a brow that has barred sleep from my eyes and lords it over me with its forbidding and its command;
by the scorpions loosed from his temples, that hasten to slay his lovers with his disdain;
by the roses of his cheeks and the myrtle of their down, the carnelian of his smiling lips and the pearls of his teeth;
by the sweetness of his breath, and the cool clear stream that runs in his mouth and puts the choicest wine and all its pressing to shame;
by his hips that quiver as he moves and as he rests, and by the slenderness of his waist;
by the bounty of his hand and the truth of his tongue, by the nobility of his stock and the height of his rank:
musk is nothing but the leavings of his beauty spot, and perfume tells its fragrance on the authority of his;
the shining sun, too, falls short of him, and the new moon I take for a paring of his fingernail.
